WEBVTT

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:31.430
We certainly would love you.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:32.290
We sure were, Tex.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:35.680
Scouts.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:37.970
The Indians didn't get our horses.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:38.820
Come on.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.110
Scouts corralled a couple of Indian ponies.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:46.910
They found a better shelter than we did.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:48.500
Pain is a beauty.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:49.660
I'll take him.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.850
Safe to head for the wagon train now, Tex.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:03.530
I'm so worried about Dad.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:04.930
You know he was badly wounded.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.410
He's probably more worried about your disappearance.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.300
We'd better get started.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.720
Before the Indians get over the freight that Titan loom gave him.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:26.290
Hawkins, you can't pull out now and leave my daughter out there at the mercy of the Indians.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:27.790
And heavens knows what.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:28.870
What do you want us to do?

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:29.970
Stay here until the Indians...

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.470
come back and scalp us all?

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.960
I know how you feel, Mr. Grant,

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.140
but as boss of this wagon frame,

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.880
I'm responsible for the lives of all of these people.

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:40.650
Now, we've waited here all night,

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.690
and we simply dare not wait any longer.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.860
But you'd think different if it was your daughter.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.090
All right, go ahead.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.430
I'll wait right here.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:49.930
I won't desert Mary.

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:51.890
Waiting won't do any good, Grant.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:53.660
You go on with the wagon frame,

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.790
and I'll lead a search party to find Mary.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.270
You keep out of this, Bart Eaton.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.450
I don't trust you, and you know it.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.600
How do you feel that way, Grant? I was only trying to help you.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:05.920
I don't know what you've got again, Eaton, Mr. Grant, but you're being unreasonable.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:09.490
He's got more at stake in this wagon train than any of us,

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.540
and I think his offer is mighty generous.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:17.070
Well, I don't want his help. If none of the rest of you'll go with me, I'll go alone.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.660
That wagon ride's easy. Put him in there, boys.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.980
Poor fellow, with all this worry, not to mention...

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:32.270
No wonder he's out of his mind.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.260
We'll try to get the legal pass before sundown.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:38.120
All right, Hogan.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:39.180
You can catch up with us, sir.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:39.520
Okay.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:41.250
You're right, everybody.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:45.190
Take good care of him, then.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:46.530
Trust me, boss.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.360
Hurry with our horses, Crosby.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:49.120
We have no time to lose.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:21.790
looks like she followed the trail of the Indians say I don't like this why should

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:25.290
we risk our scalp just because your girl run out on you it isn't only the

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:29.890
girl I'm after her brother struck it rich in the California gold field what's that

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:39.480
to us I'm cutting you all in on his mind we need the girl to get our hand that's different what are we waiting for

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:59.760
what's the matter sergeant mountain lion hexed she may be

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:05.050
Well, that old gal and the cubs will kill a lot of deer and cattle before they're through.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.470
Never argue with a woman, Bill.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:15.540
Come on, Sutton. You heard what Mary said.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:28.900
Tex, you folks can make it alone now. I've got to report to Fort Stanton.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:30.830
Good-bye, Mary.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:31.970
Good-bye, Mr. Curley.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.600
I don't know how to thank you.

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:35.120
Then don't try.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:37.470
If you keep on over that next ridge tight,

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:40.090
you'll hit Eagle Pass and save yourself several miles.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:41.660
Thanks, Bill.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:42.980
We'll do that.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:06.500
Buffalo steaks on the hoof.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:10.980
Too bad we're so far from the wagon train.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.440
They're in need of fresh meat.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:15.840
Quiet, Sutton.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:18.880
They don't even know you're here.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:23.510
I don't like the looks of that.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:25.690
They sent danger.

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:26.570
Maybe it's not.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.490
No, we're not to the wind without them.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:34.250
I thought so.

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:37.630
Indians, quick, get behind these trees.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:08:59.960
Those Indians are headed to...

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:14.220
way. Get off your horse, Mary, and keep that dog quiet. What are you going to do? There's

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:19.160
only one thing to do. I'm going to lead those Indians away from here, and you. Tax your

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:24.400
muffins. They'll kill you. Not if I reach those rocks first.

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:33.110
Come on, come on!

00:10:13.916 --> 00:10:15.916
How are you?

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:26.500
How many Indians are there?

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:29.120
You hear that, boys?

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:31.900
Don't let the Indians get Houston.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:33.710
I'll stay here with Mary.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.760
I'd have sued Eaton all right and save us the trouble.

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:06.170
Look, so Houston got away.

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:08.190
Maybe not. Let's try and find his trail.

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:08.650
Come on.

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:14.260
Start back for the wagon train.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:18.750
they'll catch up with us. I'm going to wait right here until I know Texas safe.

00:13:30.188 --> 00:13:31.068
The Indians are driving them.

00:13:31.628 --> 00:13:32.468
They're coming this way.

00:13:34.156 --> 00:13:36.296
Only chance to join Houston and the other. Come on.

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:01.460
What are you doing here?

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:02.890
Where's Eaton?

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:04.520
Here he comes now.

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:06.660
Suppose you ask him where he's been.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:08.970
That was splendid work, Houston.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.010
I'd have been in there with you if my cinch hadn't broken.

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:13.770
I tried to stop, but my horse bolted when the cinch broke.

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:14.900
I quite understand.

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:17.890
I understand Mr. Eaton. Luckily, Tex got here in time.

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:20.870
What the doot you doing Crosby?

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:23.140
Oh, just collecting a few souvenirs.

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:28.240
Let me see them.

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:30.780
Guy in.

00:16:31.788 --> 00:16:33.028
You've killed one of their chiefs.

00:16:33.452 --> 00:16:35.892
If Howlin' Wolf hears of this, he'll attack the wagon train.

00:16:36.072 --> 00:16:36.972
Now, we've got to warn them.

00:16:42.892 --> 00:16:43.272
Get mounted.

00:16:58.924 --> 00:16:59.984
Yeah, come on.

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:20.580
What do we know?

00:17:20.892 --> 00:17:22.352
That's at the top of Eagle Pass.

00:17:22.492 --> 00:17:23.252
Eagle Pass.

00:17:24.156 --> 00:17:26.456
Why, that's where Eaton said he was going to meet us with my daughter.

00:17:27.772 --> 00:17:28.472
see anything of them?

00:17:29.052 --> 00:17:29.552
Now!

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:43.380
They're all behind us.

00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:45.040
Way down at the foot of the mountain.

00:17:46.284 --> 00:17:46.784
Stop!

00:17:47.308 --> 00:17:47.848
Wait for them!

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:50.500
I can't stop on a steep grade like this.
